  "description": "Remington 870 Hardwood Home Defense (#81197, Remington Arms, 2016-2020 look). Key dimensions: overall length 38.5 in = 978 mm (remington.com / remarms.com / The Mag Life); barrel 18.5 in = 470 mm from the closed bolt face to the muzzle. The bolt face sits at the front edge of the ejection port (photos c01, c02, o02, ra02, ra03 all show the bolt filling the port with the extractor at its front end), x = 20 mm in model space; the muzzle is at x = 490 mm. The barrel object also carries the extension ring 6 mm behind the breech face, so its bbox is 476 mm. Proportions (stock length, pitch, grip, barrel, clamp, bead) follow the orthographic distributor photo i01 of #81197 scaled to 2.53 px/mm (overall length 978 mm and receiver height 62.3 mm give the same scale); o02 agrees within its perspective. Receiver about 7 13/16 in (198 mm, 16ga.com) x 1.35 in (34.3 mm) x 2.45 in (62 mm). Overall width is the forend (44 mm, assumption: no top view of #81197). Overall height runs from the recoil pad toe (z -166.3, i01: -167) to the bead top. Bore (0.729 in), magazine tube (1.00 in OD) and receiver bottom opening are sampled with axial and offset rays; the shells, follower and spring are excluded from the magazine-tube passage because the magazine is modelled loaded. max_zero_area_faces is omitted (scanfill epsilon on metre coordinates collapses the checkering and lettering micro-faces); degenerate faces are checked separately with bmesh.",
